    <!-- Manual shutter calibration -->
    <string name="row_ffc">Calibrate the shutter now</string>
    <string name="btn_start">Start</string>
    <string name="ffc_not_connected">The camera is not connected, so there is nothing to calibrate</string>
    <string name="ffc_busy">The camera is calibrating the shutter right now</string>
    <string name="ffc_requested">Shutter calibration requested</string>
    <string name="ffc_no_reaction">The camera did not start a calibration. It probably considers itself calibrated: it recalibrates by itself about every two minutes.</string>
    <string name="ffc_probe_title">Shutter calibration command</string>
    <string name="ffc_probe_message">FLIR does not publish the command that makes the camera calibrate its shutter on request, so the app has to find it. The camera calibrates itself about every two minutes and ignores the command while it thinks it is calibrated. So the app will switch the camera\'s automatic calibration off, wait until the camera asks for a calibration, then try known guesses one by one and watch whether the shutter closes (the shutter may click). Automatic calibration is always switched back on. This takes up to about 5 minutes: keep the camera plugged in and pointed at a steady scene.</string>
    <string name="ffc_probe_running">Searching for the command… The camera\'s automatic calibration is switched off for now and will be restored. This can take up to about 5 minutes.</string>
    <string name="ffc_probe_found_fmt">The shutter started in response to this command, and it is saved:\n%1$s\n\nThe button now sends it. The camera may ignore it while it considers itself calibrated.</string>
    <string name="ffc_result_not_found_fmt">The camera asked for a calibration but did not react to any of the %1$d commands tried. It still calibrates itself about every two minutes. The attempts and the camera\'s replies are in the log (USB diagnostics) for further analysis.</string>
    <string name="ffc_result_never">The camera did not ask for a calibration within about three minutes, so nothing could be tried. Automatic calibration was restored. Try again after a few more minutes of use.</string>
    <string name="ffc_result_auto">The camera went on calibrating by itself even with automatic calibration switched off, so the search could not give a reliable answer. Automatic calibration was restored.</string>
    <string name="ffc_result_send">The command could not be sent to the camera. Check the connection and try again.</string>
